@scene(400)

// Feature pruning. A part's size on screen is the wrong measure of its small
// features: this gear is 150 mm across, so it never vanishes, but its teeth
// are 1.6 mm, and from far enough away they are smaller than a pixel. A
// feature carries its own size (name.featureSize, set here by the library),
// and the viewer measures it against the pixel at the point it is looking
// at: once it is too small to see, it gives way. The gear's teeth leave its
// pitch cylinder, the circle that rolls on its mate's; the plate's 1.5 mm
// holes close and the plate reads solid; the stud's thread, crests and roots
// half a pitch across, leaves the cylinder at its pitch diameter. None is
// evaluated once gone.
//
// The band is the Detail slider's, as for parts: raise the slider and zoom
// out. Lengths are in mm.

// 150 teeth of module 1: a 150 mm pitch circle, teeth pi / 2 = 1.6 mm thick.
bigGear = max(gears.gearProfile(150.0, 1.0, radians(20.0), 0.0, 0.25, 0.05), abs(p.z) - 4.0);
bigGear.color = [0.62, 0.64, 0.68];

// A plate perforated on a 6 mm grid with 1.5 mm through holes, each one
// sized by drill.hole from its own field.
perforated = max(box([-60.0, -60.0, -3.0], [60.0, 60.0, 3.0]),
                 neg(remap(drill.hole(drill.thru(1.5), 3.0), map.patternRectangularXY([6.0, 6.0]))));
perforated.color = [0.42, 0.50, 0.62];

// An M10 x 1.5 stud 60 long, chamfered at both ends: its crests and roots are
// 0.75 mm, half the plate's holes, so the thread goes first.
stud = shaft.body([shaft.thread(10.0, 1.5, -30.0, 30.0, shaft.chamferEnd(1.0), shaft.chamferEnd(1.0))]);
stud.color = [0.70, 0.62, 0.45];

laidGear = transform.translate(bigGear, [-90.0, 0.0, 0.0]);
laidPlate = transform.translate(perforated, [90.0, 0.0, 0.0]);
return laidGear, laidPlate, stud;
